          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A river is flowing downstream at a rate of 1 km/h.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In still water Portia can swim at a rate of 2 km/h.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Portia dives into the river and swims downstream, then turns around and swims back to the starting point, taking 0.5 hours in total.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How far did she swim?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.75\\text{ km}=750\\text{ m}$ total. The downstream and upstream speeds are $3\\text{ km/h}$ and $1\\text{ km/h}$; each leg is $0.375\\text{ km}$.",
      "worked": "Downstream speed: $2+1=3\\text{ km/h}$.\n\nUpstream speed: $2-1=1\\text{ km/h}$.\n\nLet the distance swum downstream be $d$ km. The return distance is also $d$ km.\n\nTime downstream + time upstream $=0.5$ h. Using $t=\\dfrac{d}{s}$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{d}{3}+\\frac{d}{1}&=0.5\\\\\\frac{4d}{3}&=0.5\\\\4d&=1.5\\\\d&=0.375\\end{align*}$$\n\nEach leg is $0.375\\text{ km}$. Total distance swum:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2d&=2\\times0.375\\text{ km}\\\\&=0.75\\text{ km}\\\\&=750\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
